# Forward environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env*` is git-ignored except this file — never
# commit real values.
#
# Every group below fails closed: leave a group entirely empty to disable it.
# A partially filled group raises a sanitized configuration error naming only
# the missing keys, never a value.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shopify catalog (src/lib/storefront/shopify/env.ts)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both keys empty  -> deterministic static fixtures (the default; no network).
# Both keys set    -> live Shopify catalog mode.
# Only one set     -> ShopifyConfigurationError. There is no partial mode.
#
# Catalog reads are server-owned and use the private token with Hydrogen's
# `private_no_buyer_context` client. PRIVATE_STOREFRONT_API_TOKEN must never
# reach browser code, props, logs, errors, tests, or Git.

PUBLIC_STORE_DOMAIN=your-shop.myshopify.com
PRIVATE_STOREFRONT_API_TOKEN=

# Optional. Which Shopify menu feeds the Header. Defaults to `main-menu`.
PUBLIC_MAIN_MENU_HANDLE=main-menu

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Customer Account (src/lib/account/env.ts)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All four keys empty -> account integration disabled, and the account
# surfaces render their signed-out prototype states.
# All four set        -> Shopify Customer Account mode.
# Anything else       -> ShopifyConfigurationError. The tuple is all-or-none.
#
# PUBLIC_STOREFRONT_ORIGIN is the single origin source for OAuth callback
# construction, refresh, logout, and return-target validation. Request `Host`,
# `Forwarded`, and `X-Forwarded-Host` headers are never origin inputs, so this
# must be the real deployed origin.
#
# CUSTOMER_ACCOUNT_SESSION_SECRET needs at least 32 bytes of CSPRNG material:
#   openssl rand -base64 32

SHOP_ID=
PUBLIC_CUSTOMER_ACCOUNT_API_CLIENT_ID=
CUSTOMER_ACCOUNT_SESSION_SECRET=
PUBLIC_STOREFRONT_ORIGIN=https://your-deployment.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Weaverse (@weaverse/next)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Install only an exact registry-verified version. The npm `latest` tag is
# stale (0.1.0-alpha.0); the `alpha` tag resolved to 0.1.0-alpha.16 on
# 2026-09-08. Re-verify at install time.

# Required for Weaverse page/theme data.
WEAVERSE_PROJECT_ID=

# Optional. Defaults to https://studio.weaverse.io inside the SDK. Set only to
# point at a dev or staging Studio host.
WEAVERSE_HOST=

# Optional. Not needed for public page/theme loading. Set only for approved
# Content API work.
WEAVERSE_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reserved — not read by the running app
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLIC_STOREFRONT_API_TOKEN and PUBLIC_STOREFRONT_ID are deliberately not
# read by the storefront. Catalog reads use the private token instead, and the
# public token stays reserved for a future client/Studio/ShopifyScripts slice.
#
# They are read today only by the opt-in verification scripts
# (`bun run verify:shopify`) and by the credential matrices in
# `scripts/env-matrix.mts`.
#
# Note before wiring @weaverse/next: the SDK surfaces PUBLIC_STORE_DOMAIN and
# PUBLIC_STOREFRONT_API_TOKEN to the browser through its `publicEnv` payload.
# Public-token browser use is outside the current approval in AGENTS.md, so
# setting PUBLIC_STOREFRONT_API_TOKEN once composition is wired is a decision
# to make deliberately, not a default.

PUBLIC_STOREFRONT_API_TOKEN=
PUBLIC_STOREFRONT_ID=
